{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When they had finished eating.</b> Judah said to them: Wait for the old man until the bread is used up from the house (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>When they had finished.</b> כַּד שֵׁצִיאוּ, and the translator [who rendered] כַּד סַפִּיקוּ is mistaken — ״כַּאֲשֶׁר כִּלּוּ הַגְּמַלִּים לִשְׁתּוֹת״ rendered כַּד סַפִּיקוּ means: when they had drunk their fill, that is the completion of their drinking; but this one, ״כַּאֲשֶׁר כִּלּוּ לֶאֱכֹל״ — it means when the food was gone, and we render כַּד שֵׁצִיאוּ."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:18.553605347Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}